                <pb facs="0455" n="353" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg353"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">5727/253.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Spanish
                    Minister.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-09-30"><hi rendition="#italic">September 30,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 24th instant, advising the department that the Spanish
                    chambers of commerce are under the direct supervision of your Government, being
                    placed under the ministry of fomento.</p>
                <p>In reply I have the honor to inform you that the department has taken pleasure in
                    communicating this information to the Department of the Treasury for its
                    information and action. The department will advise you, upon notification by the
                    Department of the Treasury, of its decision in the matter.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Bacon.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
